      "kind": {
        "text": "This one never needed the borrow, which is why it fell first. `Int.mul` on mixed signs produces `Int.negOfNat k`, a `Nat.rec` stuck on `k`; a triple product leaves one under a second multiplication in six of its eight branches. Four lemmas unstick it -- `ofNat m * negOfNat k = negOfNat (m*k)` and the three other placements -- and each is a two-case split whose branches close by `Eq.refl` or one `Nat.zero_mul`. After that every branch is `Nat.mul_assoc` wrapped in `ofNat` when the number of negative factors is even and `negOfNat` when it is odd. `formal.statement` is `Kernel::render_lean` of the admitted type, verbatim from `int_theorem_inventory`.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
